  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Quiet weather period with warming trend this week.\n\nClouds in the northwest flow are going to fade east of the\nmountains this afternoon/evening, and eventually start to\nclear/scatter out Monday across the western slopes as airmass\ngets progressively drier. Just some very light returns on radar\nin the west this afternoon, so don't be surprised if you see a\nsnowflake/sprinkle/drizzle in the mountains. High pressure\nbuilds in for the rest of the week. 500mb heights will slowly \nincrease as well and lead to progressively warmer days each day\nthroughout the work week. Highs Monday will generally be near \naverage or slightly below average in the 40s/50s across the \narea, with widespread 60s to near 70 overtaking the area by \nmidweek. While daytime highs will warm up to these temperatures,\nclear skies and calm winds will allow for efficient radiational\ncooling each night with some lows in the 20s and gradually \n\"warming\" into the 30s.",
